  "p2cdb007f": "<p><strong>A. Click Sales-&gt;Sales Transaction</strong></p>  <p><strong>B. How to sale item?</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Easy Steps:</p> <p>1. Click Sales-&gt;<strong>Sales Transaction</strong></p> <p>2. Select <strong>Table</strong> (when Sales Config <strong>Has Table</strong> is yes). A vacant table starts a new order; a table with an order opens that order.</p> <p>3. Select <strong>Category</strong></p> <p>4. Select <strong>Item</strong> - one click adds quantity 1 (a quantity window opens when Sales Config <strong>PopupQty</strong> is yes)</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;...repeat the process until all items entered</p> <p>5. Choose <strong>DINE IN</strong> or <strong>TAKE OUT</strong></p> <p>6. Click <strong>SEND</strong> to send the order to the kitchen (the kitchen slip, the Kitchen Queue or both: see Sales Config-&gt;Send Kitchen). Items already sent are not sent again.</p> <p>7. Click <strong>SERVE</strong> when the order is served to the customer.</p> <p>8. Click <strong>BILL OUT</strong> to print the bill (optional).</p> <p>9. Click <strong>PAY</strong>-&gt;Input <strong>AmountPaid</strong>-&gt;Press Enter / Click Save</p> <p>10. Click <strong>COMPLETE</strong> to make the table available for the next transaction.</p>  <p><strong>C. Tabs and buttons</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>TABLE CATEGORY</strong> (when Files Config <strong>MultipleTable</strong> is yes), <strong>TABLE</strong>, <strong>CATEGORY</strong> and <strong>PRODUCT</strong> - choose the table area, the table, the category and the item. Press F8 to go to the <strong>PRODUCT</strong> tab: the search box and <strong>HIDE PRICE</strong> (hide the prices) work on that tab.</li> <li><strong>SEND</strong> - sends the new items to the kitchen. <strong>SERVE</strong> - marks the order as served.</li> <li><strong>READY TO SERVE</strong> - shows how many tables have items ready from the kitchen. Click it to see the tables, click <strong>View details</strong> to see their items, then click <strong>Served</strong> (or <strong>Serve All</strong>). <strong>Back</strong> returns to the tables.</li> <li><strong>UPGRADE</strong> - select a Set item, click <strong>UPGRADE</strong> and choose the component to replace with another item. The new item is charged its own price less the price of the replaced item (you can edit it) and stays with the Set.</li> <li><strong>TRANSFER</strong> - click <strong>TRANSFER</strong>, then select the vacant table to move the order to.</li> <li><strong>MERGE</strong> - click <strong>MERGE</strong>, then select the table whose bill is added to this one.</li> <li><strong>SPLIT</strong> - see D.</li> <li><strong>LOAD S.O</strong> and <strong>POINTS</strong> - shown when your access rights allow them.</li> </ul>  <p><strong>D. How to split the bill?</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Easy Steps:</p> <p>1. Open the table-&gt;Click <strong>SPLIT</strong></p> <p>2. Choose <strong>BY ITEMS</strong> - tick the items to pay, or <strong>BY AMOUNT</strong> - input the amount to pay</p> <p>3. Click <strong>PAY</strong> - only the split part is paid and the rest stays on the table. Click <strong>SPLIT</strong> again to cancel.</p> <ul> <li>BY AMOUNT takes whole items in order and cuts the rest by quantity from one item. Set items and items not yet sent to the kitchen are not cut, so the paid amount can be slightly different; it is shown before paying.</li> </ul>  <p><strong>E. How to cancel an item or the order?</strong></p> <ul> <li>RightClick the item-&gt;<strong>Edit</strong>, <strong>Remove</strong>, <strong>Remove All</strong> or <strong>Cancel Order</strong>.</li> <li>Use <strong>Cancel Order</strong> for items already sent to the kitchen: the CANCELLED slip is printed or the Kitchen Queue is told, depending on Send Kitchen.</li> </ul>  <p><strong>F. A table shows an amount but opens empty?</strong></p> <ul> <li>The order was left by another cashier or by an earlier reading. Click the table: the system shows who has it, the reading, the time and the amount, and offers to release the table.</li> <li>Confirm with the password to cancel that order and make the table vacant.</li> </ul>  <p>On a phone see Web Version-&gt;Using a Phone or Tablet.</p>",
