  "pbc745f85": "<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A. Click</strong> <strong>Files-&gt;Printers</strong></p> <ul> <ul> <li>New&nbsp;- to add new printer <li>Edit - to&nbsp;edit printer&nbsp; <li>Delete - to delete printer </li></ul></ul> <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; B. How to add new printer? </strong></p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Easy Steps:</p> <blockquote> <p>1. Click Files-&gt;<strong>Printer</strong></p> <p>2. Click <strong>New</strong> button</p> <p>3. Locate PrinterName</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;In the Windows taskbar, search for <strong>Printers &amp; Scanners</strong> and open it.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Browse through the list of printers connected to your network and select the one you want to add.</p> <p> 4. Fill in the Printer Details</p><p> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Area - Enter the location of the printer (e.g., \"Office 1\" or \"Reception\").</p> <p> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;PrinterName - Enter the exact name of the printer as listed in your computer.</p></blockquote> <p> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 5. Click<strong>Save </strong><strong> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;C. How to edit/delete printer? </strong></p> <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong><strong>&nbsp; </strong>Easy Steps:</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1. Search Printer</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2. Click <strong>Edit</strong> button for edit and <strong>Delete button</strong> for delete.</p>  <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; D. How to view assigned items&nbsp;for a printer?</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong><strong>&nbsp; </strong>Easy Steps:</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;1. <strong>Select a Printer</strong>: Choose a printer from the first panel.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2. <strong>View Assigned Items</strong>: The second panel will display all items currently assigned to the selected printer.</p>  <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; E. How to remove/remove all assigned items&nbsp;from a printer?</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong><strong>&nbsp; </strong>Easy Steps:</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1. <strong>Select a Printer</strong>: Choose a printer from the first panel.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2. <strong>View Assigned Items</strong>: The second panel will display all items currently assigned to the selected printer.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 3. Click <strong>Remove</strong> or <strong>Remove</strong> <strong>All</strong> button to remove item from printer.</p>  <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; F. How to assign items&nbsp;to a printer?</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong><strong>&nbsp; </strong>Easy Steps:</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1. <strong>Select a Printer</strong>: Choose a printer from the first panel.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2. <strong>View Assigned Items</strong>: The second panel will display all items currently assigned to the selected printer.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 3. <strong>View Unassigned Items</strong>: Click the <strong>View</strong> button in the third panel to see items not assigned to any printer.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 4. <strong>Select Items</strong>: Check the boxes next to the items you want to assign to the selected printer.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 5. <strong>Select All Items</strong>: Use the <strong>Check All</strong> button to select all items at once.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 6. <strong>Filter by Category</strong>: Choose a category to view items specific to that category.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 7. <strong>Assign Items</strong>: Click the <strong>Assign</strong> button to complete the process.</p>",
