  "pd9a20eef": "<p>1. <a data-page=\"web_version.htm\">Web Version</a></p> <p>2. <a data-page=\"page_58.html\">Files</a></p> <p>3. <a data-page=\"Menus.htm\">Menus</a></p> <p>4. <a data-page=\"page_62.html\">Inventory</a></p> <p>5. <a data-page=\"page_77.html\">Sales</a></p> <p>6. <a data-page=\"page_107.html\">Cashiering</a></p> <p>7. <a data-page=\"page_111.html\">Receiving</a></p> <p>8. <a data-page=\"page_140.html\">Expenses</a></p> <p>9. <a data-page=\"returns_group.htm\">Returns</a></p> <p>10. <a data-page=\"page_181.html\">Reports</a></p> <p>11. <a data-page=\"page_185.html\">Accounting</a></p> <p>12. <a data-page=\"page_193.html\">Access Rights</a></p>",
  "pdb50db38": "<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A. Click</strong> Menu <strong>-&gt;Menu Costing</strong></p> <ul> <ul> <li>View - to view items for costing&nbsp; <li>Components- set up menu costing <li>Print - to print items for costing</li></ul></ul>  <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; B. </strong><strong>Filter by ItemType</strong>: Choose a item type to view items specific to that item type.</p>  <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; C. How to set up menu costing?</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Easy Steps:</p> <blockquote> <p>1. Select Item and Add <strong>Components</strong> </p> <p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>Choose the item to cost, then click <strong>Components</strong>.</p> <p>2. Click <strong>View </strong>button from first panel to view unassigned components.</p> <p>3. Add <strong> Ingredients</strong> and <strong> Quantity</strong> </p><p> <strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Select all required <strong> ingredients</strong> .</p> <p> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Set<strong>QtyMade</strong> based on expected output.</p><p> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; For each ingredients input<strong>QtyUsed</strong> based on<strong> QtyMade</strong> amount.</p> <p> 4. Adjust Unit of Measure ( <strong> UM</strong>) </p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If UM differs between receiving and costing, double-click UM to adjust.</p> <p> 5. Calculate<strong> Cost</strong> </p> <p> <strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>The system will auto-calculate the<strong> cost</strong> per finished product.</p> <p> 6. Set<strong> Price</strong></p> <p> <strong> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Close, then click the <strong>Price</strong> column to edit.</p><p> 7. Ready for<strong> Transaction</strong> </p></blockquote><p><strong> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; D. How to remove/remove all assigned components?</strong> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </p><p> <strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong> <strong> &nbsp;</strong>Easy Steps: </p> <p> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1.<strong>Select a Component</strong>: Choose a component from the second panel.</p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2. Click <strong> Remove</strong> or <strong> Remove</strong> <strong> All</strong> button to remove item from printer.</p>  <p><strong>E. Web version</strong></p> <ul> <li>When items are received (Receiving Transaction) the costing of the menu is updated automatically: a component that is received at a higher cost than the menu uses takes the new cost, and the cost of the menu is computed again. A lower cost never reduces the cost of a menu. Every change is kept in the menu costing history.</li> </ul>",
